   "reference": {
    "title": "WHO 5th cutaneous melanoma & AJCC 8th microstaging",
    "intro": "Report Breslow thickness to the nearest 0.1 mm (not 0.01 mm). In AJCC 8th, pT1 splits at 0.8 mm (pT1a < 0.8 mm non-ulcerated; pT1b < 0.8 mm ulcerated or 0.8–1.0 mm); mitotic rate is still required for prognosis but no longer governs pT1a/b.",
    "note": "Photomicrographs are from Wikimedia Commons under open Creative Commons licences. ExpertPath pages open with your own ExpertPath login; the app holds none of their images.",
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "Microstaging, microsatellites & molecular testing",
      "points": [
       "Breslow thickness is measured from the top of the granular layer (or base of ulcer) to the deepest invasive melanoma cell (excluding adventitial/adnexal extension and microsatellites).",
       "Microsatellites (any discontinuous dermal/subcutaneous nest separated from main tumour by normal tissue), satellites, or in-transit metastases upstage N to pN1c (0 nodes), pN2c (1 node), or pN3c (>= 2 nodes).",
       "IHC/molecular: SOX10, S100, Melan-A, HMB45, PRAME; test BRAF V600E/K (and NRAS/KIT for acral/high-CSD) on stage III/IV or high-risk resected disease."
      ],
      "links": [
       {
        "label": "ExpertPath: Cutaneous Melanoma",
        "url": "https://app.expertpath.com/"
       }
      ],
